From e488d3af4db8666b90c019361bcaffbc694c31f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayesh Rathod <jayesh4.rathod@ril.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 13:20:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] Purge terminal symbols from current scanner state,
 preserving history

Step 7 of the Cross-Scanner Eligibility and Corporate Lifecycle Sprint.

The gateway stops a terminal symbol entering a new scan, but state files already
on disk can reintroduce one as a current candidate. This adds a date-aware
cleaner rather than a per-ticker blacklist, so it works for the next merger too.

The rule
--------
* A symbol recorded against a session *before* its terminal date was validly
  observed then. That record is history and is left alone.
* A symbol recorded against a session *on or after* its terminal date is
  defective output and is removed.

For JBCHEPHARM the boundary is 2026-07-17, the session after its last trade on
2026-07-16. Every occurrence in the shipped state files turned out to be dated
2026-07-22 or later, so all 21 were defective rather than historical:

  old_nse_hull_shadow_state.json             1 session  [2026-08-19]
  old_nse_hull_historical_replay_state.json 20 sessions [2026-07-22 .. 2026-08-18]

Price history is untouched: JBCHEPHARM remains in 395 files under
market_data/daily/, and in the corporate snapshots, exactly as required.

Positions are not silently deleted. An open position in a terminal symbol is a
portfolio event -- a corporate conversion or a terminal exit -- and belongs to
v2/universe_reconciliation, which the scanners now run. The script reports such
positions and refuses to touch them. None were found.

Safety
------
Dry run is the default; --apply writes and keeps a .bak of each file. Re-running
is a no-op. A regression test asserts the repository's own state files stay
clean, so this cannot silently reappear.

Tests: 12 new, including explicit assertions that 2026-07-16 survives and
2026-07-17 does not, and that an undated structure is never edited.

Note for applying this patch: if the two state-file hunks conflict with your
CI's auto-persisted state, drop them and run
  python scripts/purge_terminal_symbols_from_state.py --apply
which produces the same result.
